Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.

The Community You Will Join:

The Airbnb Hotels team is a fun, fast-growing group leading Airbnb’s expansion into the hotel sector. Operating with an entrepreneurial spirit, this team combines the simplicity, product excellence, and guest-centered ethos that define Airbnb. This team’s mission is to deliver the smoothest, most intuitive hotel booking experience for guests, while helping hotels easily drive incremental bookings so they can focus on delivering the best hospitality. The ultimate aim is to help more people discover high-quality hotels, creating value for guests and our hotel partners.

&nbsp;

The Difference You Will Make:

&nbsp;

As a Senior Enterprise Account Manager, your primary focus will be to drive new Enterprise acquisition and successfully onboard and optimize partnerships with regional or global hotel groups. Your focus will be to enhance Airbnb's market presence through collaboration with other teams, leveraging your expertise in your regional market and enterprise account&nbsp; partnerships. With a deep understanding of Airbnb's mission and values, you will oversee all aspects of supply acquisition and partner success. This includes developing acquisition strategies, generating and converting Hotel Group leads, and managing relationships with strategic partners, including the creation of new partnerships. You will also be tasked with developing and refining scalable, regionalized or global supply management strategies for both established, competitive markets and emerging, untapped markets, aiming to secure our long-term success in these regions.

&nbsp;

A Typical Day:

&nbsp;

• Own the end-to-end lifecycle of newly acquired Enterprise partnerships, from lead to successful optimization.&nbsp;

• Execute a global win-win strategy for your portfolio that drives value to all parties and positions Airbnb and HotelTonight as a top strategic partner across all distribution channels.

• Through the creation of mutual account plans with your partners you will deliver Objectives and KPIs that support the goals of Airbnb and our Enterprise Partners

• Negotiate agreements with Enterprise partners to unlock new opportunities for both parties &amp; promote long term mutual success

• Leverage data to make decisions and design projects to best expand and enhance availability and revenue through existing partnerships.

• Monitor &amp; analyze over/underperformance, market trends, growth opportunities or anomalies and regularly communicate performance to Executives leveraging available production data and global market insight.

• Work with partners to ensure that the partnership is held to the highest industry standards and that commercial agreements as well as SLAs are met.

• Develop close working relationships with key internal teams and individuals to ensure that they&nbsp; provide appropriate levels of support to these key partnerships and key enhancements are made to unlock revenue for the business.

• Conduct regular business reviews, formal presentations for internal and external purposes.

• Work cross-functionally to execute changes at scale while collaborating with Market Management as a subject matter expert in Enterprise accounts to drive local property performance.&nbsp;

• Proactively contribute to the development and standardization of Enterprise team processes, playbooks, and best practices across the global function

&nbsp;

Your Expertise:

&nbsp;

• 8+ years of Enterprise/Strategic Partnerships Account Management experience

• Deep understanding of the travel industry and an extensive network within the Hospitality ecosystem in APAC&nbsp;

Location:&nbsp; This position may be performed remotely but requires flexibility and a willingness to travel as needed. &nbsp;

Position Summary &nbsp;

The Commercial Engineer leads end-to-end operation of the brand’s commercial model, ensuring strategy, workflows, systems, people, and data work together to support effective execution. You will set the standard for how the commercial organization operates, continually monitor and challenge the brand’s operating model and strategic assumptions, make evidence-based recommendations, and partner with senior leaders across Commercial, Medical Affairs, Market Access, Trade &amp; Distribution, and Finance to improve results, acting with urgency whenever brand performance is at risk.&nbsp; &nbsp;

Primary Responsibilities &nbsp;

• Own end-to-end operations for the brand.&nbsp; Lead the design and completion of the commercial build and serve as the organization’s authority on the strategy, workflows, systems, vendors, and data that support the brand. Define and lead the vision for commercial excellence.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Drive operational performance - Define and own the integrated view of how the brand operates, tracking performance against goals and surfacing risks before they escalate. &nbsp;

• Diagnose and resolve cross-functional issues - Partner with senior functional leaders, up to and including the leadership team, to align on priorities, identify issues and root causes, and drive timely resolution, sharing accountability for outcomes and acting with urgency when commercial performance is at risk. &nbsp;

• Challenge and improve the operating model - Continuously question strategic assumptions and existing processes, using evidence-based analysis to recommend improvements that strengthen commercial performance. Present recommendations directly to leadership team. &nbsp;

• Shape strategy through business insights- Lead the research and intelligence agenda in partnership with cross-functional leaders, translating market dynamics, competitor activity, and emerging trends into actionable recommendations that inform strategic decisions and strengthen commercial performance. &nbsp;

• Lead without authority at scale - Direct the work of matrixed, cross-functional teams and external vendors on the highest-impact commercial initiatives, such as launch readiness and operating-model redesign, without formal direct reports. &nbsp;

Qualifications and Key Success Factors &nbsp;

• Bachelor's degree required; with extensive experience in pharma/biotech commercial operations, brand management, consulting, or related commercial/strategic roles &nbsp;

• Recognized expertise in how commercial strategy, data, systems, workflows, and vendors come together to drive brand performance across a commercial portfolio &nbsp;

• Strategic, analytical problem solver who sees across functions, brings clarity to complex issues, identifies root causes, and translates evidence into actionable recommendations-following through until issues are resolved. High ownership and urgency; steps into ambiguity, challenges assumptions, and acts when performance is at risk &nbsp;

• Credible, collaborative influencer who can align and challenge executive and senior cross-functional leaders, including the leadership team, without relying on authority &nbsp;

• Curious, resilient, and constantly looking for a better way to operate and deliver results &nbsp;

• The physical and mental requirements of our roles include but are not limited to regular use of a computer, devices or other office equipment, clear communication, and occasional movement. You'll need comfort with screen work, basic hand coordination, and focus. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform these functions. &nbsp;

